Why these belong in the archive rather than in the bin: draft 1's two failures were fixture defects
(an all-`a` digest has zero entropy so no rule can fire, and a one-line `{"path": "<hex>"}` does not
trip the keyword-adjacency the rule needs) plus a control that was not legal gitleaks (a
[[allowlists]] block with zero checks aborts the run, so the control drops the whole block). Draft
2's two failures were one wrong theory held twice: that generic-api-key's value class is
lowercase-only. The final arm [6] settles it -- the same 36-character body with the ghp_ prefix
stripped IS reported, so the prefix is what that rule skips, in both spellings. A quiet scan would
have hidden all of this; only the differential showed it.
